Developer Workflow
Version: 2026-07-20
Status: Authoritative Developer Guide

Overview
This document explains how to work on the WordList Writer codebase. It merges the original developer workflow with updated architecture rules, tokenizer rules, rendering rules, highlight pipeline rules, startup sequence rules, and July 19 fixes. It is designed for future developers and future sessions that need to reconstruct the internal architecture, pipelines, and coding conventions. It follows the GitHub-safe formatting rules used across the project.

1. Architecture Overview
WordList Writer consists of four major layers:
* UI Layer (HTML, CSS, JS)
* Analysis Layer (tokenizer, normalization, highlight pipeline)
* Curriculum Layer (Master List, Project List, Cognates, Frequency)
* Backend Layer (Express plus Supabase)
The system uses static JSON files for linguistic data, a lightweight Express server, and Supabase for persistence.

2. Folder Structure
The project uses the following folder layout:
* src/controllers
* src/lib
* src/routes
* src/utils
* public/frequency
* public/lemmas
* public/cognates
* public/master
* public/master/backups
* docs
* scripts
Folder purposes:
* controllers: backend logic for API routes
* lib: shared backend utilities such as Supabase client and normalization helpers
* routes: Express route definitions
* utils: frontend utilities such as tokenizer and highlight logic
* public: static JSON data and client-side assets
* docs: full documentation suite
* scripts: maintenance scripts

3. Frontend Pipeline Overview
The frontend pipeline processes text in the following order:
* tokenize text
* normalize lemmas
* lookup cognates
* lookup frequency
* lookup curriculum rank
* determine highlight class
* update project list
* update violations panel
* render UI
All steps must remain in this order. Rendering must occur only through requestHighlightUpdate.

4. Tokenizer Workflow
Tokenizer responsibilities:
* split text into tokens
* preserve punctuation
* preserve whitespace
* handle contractions
* return array of token objects for words
* return raw strings for punctuation and whitespace
Rules:
* must not trigger highlight or autosave
* must not log normalized tokens
Location:
src/utils/tokenizer.js

5. Normalization Workflow
Normalization ensures consistent lemma handling.
Rules:
* lowercase
* Unicode NFD
* strip diacritics
* remove punctuation
Location:
src/utils/normalizeLemma.js

6. Highlight Pipeline
Highlighting uses priority rules:
* cognate: green underline
* known: normal
* unknown: red asterisk
Rules:
* all highlight operations must enter through requestHighlightUpdate
* handleStableInput must never be called directly from event listeners
* requestHighlightUpdate uses debounce
* no highlight during IME composition
Location:
src/utils/highlight.js
Dependencies:
* masterSet
* frequencySet
* cognateMap
* tokenizer
* normalizeLemma

7. Project List Workflow
Project List tracks all lemmas in the current text.
Rules:
* normalized lemmas only
* no duplicates
* update dynamically as text changes
* must not trigger highlight
Location:
src/utils/projectList.js

8. Master List Workflow
Master List defines curriculum order.
Rules:
* unique lemmas
* unique ranks
* normalized lemmas
* plain strings only
* cross-language equivalents allowed
Location:
src/utils/masterList.js

9. Violations Workflow
Violations detect curriculum issues.
Types:
* unknown word
* out-of-order word
* curriculum gap
Rules:
* must run after highlight on startup
Location:
src/utils/violations.js

